## Summary

I delivered the **`TelemetryGrid`** Apple/SwiftUI feature-view surface (P4 · 0285) as a production-quality parity port of `web/.../telemetry-panels/TelemetryGrid.tsx`, committed as `95eb15f6c` (9 files, 1779 lines).

**Surface (mirrors sibling `VehicleStatePanel`/0287, composes shared `InfoTile`/0280):**
- 6-tile adaptive grid (Battery, Speed, Inside, Odometer, Charger, Sentry) via `LazyVGrid` + per-cell `TSStaggerItem` (web `StaggerItem` cascade)
- `useUnits` ports (SI m→km/mi, m/s→km/h·mph, °C→°C/°F, `fmtInt`/`fmtNumber`), pure testable projection, P1/S8 state-holder seam (no I/O in the view), P1/S10 i18n facade (zero English literals), P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry
- All P4 states render: loading / empty / error / data / **stale / offline**; full VoiceOver + Dynamic Type + reduce-motion support

**Verification (real evidence):**
- `swiftlint --strict` 0 violations · `swiftformat --lint` clean · placeholder gate 0
- Isolated `swiftc -typecheck` against the **iOS 18 simulator SDK (Swift 6)**: surface, previews, and tests all **EXIT=0**
- Native **runtime execution** of the formatting/projection logic: `ALL_RUNTIME_CHECKS_PASSED` (every value/tone/sub matches the web spec exactly)
- The isolated check even caught & fixed a real Swift 6 concurrency bug in my own tests

**Gate status — `STATUS=BLOCKED` (EXIT=65), with platform-capability evidence as the prompt permits:** The full-scheme `xcodebuild build test` cannot reach 0 on this runner for reasons entirely outside my allowed scope — confirmed via `git status` (only my 9 untracked files changed):
- **iOS:** the baseline app target doesn't compile under Xcode 26.5 / Swift 6.3 — ~59 pre-existing sibling files use a non-`@escaping` `@ViewBuilder` helper, plus a swift-frontend **IRGen crash** in `AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift`
- **macOS:** fails at code-signing (no development certificate provisioned)

I deliberately did **not** edit the ~59 out-of-scope sibling surfaces (owned by other prompts) to force a green gate. The committed log records the true failure causes and the isolated-verification evidence — no red was reported as green.

